  "articleBody": "It's tough when your car gets banged up in an accident, especially when it's not your fault. The first thing you'll want to do, after ensuring everyone's safety, is document everything. Take lots of photos and videos of the scene, damage to all vehicles involved, and any visible injuries. Exchange information with the other driver, but keep conversations brief and stick to facts. Don't admit fault or apologize, even if you feel bad – that can be misinterpreted later. Once you're safe, report the accident to your insurance company. They'll start the process, but remember their primary goal is to minimize their payout. This is where an experienced attorney, like Angelo Reyes, can really help you navigate the complexities of property damage recovery. We can help assess the full extent of your vehicle's damage and ensure you're not getting short-changed by the insurance company, especially in places like Carlsbad or San Diego where accidents are common. Getting a professional involved early can make a big difference in the outcome of your claim.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
}